n, durability and proper installation matter, too.\n\n  * Buy from a reputable manufacturer. Chezem recommends buying babyproofing gear from a reputable manufacturer with clear US contact information and information about the safety standard the product meets rather than vague language like “meets all safety standards.” Red flags: a marketplace seller that’s a random string of letters or numbers (instead of an actual brand) and pricing that’s too good to be true.\n\n  * Recalls and registration. Check the CPSC’s Recalls and Product Safety Warnings site for any product recalls before you buy or use any babyproofing gear. Register eligible baby gear so you'll be contacted if it's recalled later.\n\n  * Pay special attention to safety gates. Gates must meet a mandatory federal safety standard. A legitimate gate should carry third-party testing, a tracking label and a registration card in the box.\n\nYou can also look for products carrying the Baby Safety Alliance verified seal. It can be found on a product’s packaging and indicates the item meets the highest federal, state and voluntary safety standards set for its category.\n\n### Reassess as your baby grows \n\nJust like parenting, babyproofing isn’t something you do once and never think about again. Revisit your setup as your baby’s abilities change. \n\n  * Check that gates and locks still work.\n\n  * Look for new hazards as your baby learns to climb.\n\n  * Routinely scan your home for anything that’s crept back within reach.\n\nAnd don’t forget to babyproof beyond your own home. Sitters’ and grandparents’ homes, hotel rooms and vacation rentals all need to be babyproofed if you’re spending time there. \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBaby Proofing Products Online in Bahrain | Centrepoint (https://www.centrepointstores.com/bh/en/c/baby-healthandsafety-babyproofing)\nciteturn88search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; \nMunchkin\n\nMunchkin Portable Baby Soo